alias ExitStatus = std::process::ExitStatus;
alias Inputs = std::process::Inputs;

public fn main(inputs: Inputs) -> status: ExitStatus pure waits doc "firn, a server of Redis's protocol: PING, ECHO, GET, SET with EX or PX, MSET, INCR, DEL, EXISTS, TYPE, EXPIRE, PEXPIRE, PEXPIREAT, TTL, PTTL, PERSIST, DBSIZE, CONFIG GET, the lists' LPUSH, RPUSH, LPOP, RPOP, LRANGE and LLEN, the sets' SADD, SREM, SPOP and SCARD, the hashes' HSET and HGET and the sorted sets' ZADD, ZPOPMIN, ZCARD and ZSCORE, over TCP in RESP2 or as inline commands, with pipelining. It listens on the loopback port the first argument names and serves each accepted client in a context of its own over one keyspace, a shared object every client reaches through atomic statements. The second argument is how many clients to accept; zero accepts until the listener fails. A third argument other than - names an append-only file in the working directory: firn replays it before it listens and appends every change to it, syncing it once a second. A fourth argument, when not zero, closes a client silent for that many seconds. Expired keys are removed when a command finds them and by a context that wakes ten times a second.";
